{"step_index":3578,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:54:10Z","thinking":"Experimentation reveals a hard payload limit around 64KB, triggering errors beyond approximately 250 items. Observed performance degradation and shifts to summary/code interpretation occur between 150-200 items. Optimal performance, indicated by rapid response times and consistent JSON output, is found around 75 items, corresponding to roughly 20KB payload size and a significant reduction in overall message count.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Update walkthrough with 75-item optimal batching and 413 resolution\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Walkthrough: Parallel Processing, Resilient Extraction, Gemini Fallback & Production Deployment\\n\\nAll requested enhancements, bug fixes, parallel performance optimizations, and production packaging have been implemented and verified end-to-end.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Parallel Multi-Threaded File Extraction (المعالجة المتوازية للملفات)\\n- **Problem**: Previously, files were uploaded and processed sequentially one-by-one. When processing multiple warehouse catalogs (e.g. 6 PDFs), the total time accumulated to over 30 minutes, and any single network timeout aborted all remaining files.\\n- **Solution (`src/extract/file_handler.py`)**:\\n  - Implemented `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=min(len(filepaths), 8))`.\\n  - All warehouse files (PDF, Excel, JSON) are now dispatched concurrently in parallel threads.\\n  - The Unstructured API accepts concurrent requests, allowing all cloud extraction jobs to run simultaneously.\\n  - Finished files are returned, saved, and cached independently as soon as they complete.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. 22-Page Hadaba PDF Resolution (`الهضبة الاثنين نقدى0.pdf`)\\n- **Problem**: \\n  - The 22-page Hadaba PDF document timed out on synchronous HTTP requests (> 16 minutes), and when it completed, Unstructured returned 0 items because the data was formatted as an HTML `<table>` in `markdown` rather than `extracted_data`.\\n- **Solution (`src/extract/pdf_reader.py`)**:\\n  - Extended polling timeout to 24 minutes (180 attempts × 8s) with an initial 20-second fast-wait to prevent hanging synchronous sockets.\\n  - Enhanced `parse_structured_result()`:\\n    1. First inspects schema `extracted_data`.\\n    2. If empty or absent, parses HTML `<table><tr><td>...</td></tr></table>` directly from `result[\\\"markdown\\\"]` with automatic column detection (Arabic column headers like `اسم الصنف`, `اسم الدواء`).\\n  - **Result**: Successfully extracted **1,071 drug items** with full names, strengths, and pack sizes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Resilience & Automatic Gemini 3.6 Flash \n<truncated 3137 bytes>","Description":"\"Update walkthrough with 75-batch and 413 fix\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\kakak\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\\\walkthrough.md\"","toolAction":"\"Update walkthrough.md\"","toolSummary":"\"Document 75-item batch optimization\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
